{"c":[{"id":"07973d9b178b6e96","sum":"v1, B1-B12: never commit .scratch/ or SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN; screenpipe@0.4.50 :3031 /search needs Bearer key + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; Chrome's titled AXWebArea stays out of keys; don't edit a running bash script; never mutate w.nodes; Jev text goes via a SnippetLedger.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"55288e90aa520159","sum":"v1: .scratch/ never committed; Screenpipe sidecar (own screenpipe@0.4.50 :3031) behind hard-failing last-N; /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN; CI macos-26; skills JSON in caret/skills/<id>/.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"79ee0e2da00c6468","sum":"v1: .scratch/ never committed; Screenpipe sidecar behind a hard-failing last-N facade; Supabase control plane only; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN. CI keeps macos-26 (macos-15 type-checks #available). Caret.app runs own screenpipe@0.4.50 :3031; no CaretProjectRoot: no-op.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fb9536a9c704d4b7","sum":"Repo and v1 lore: SumMem at .summem/summem; .scratch/ never committed; v1 kept five upstreams, Screenpipe a supervised sidecar (launcher lease) behind a last-N facade that hard-fails when down or empty; Supabase is control plane only; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e2a432b193b2a33","sum":"Repo setup and v1 lore: SumMem at .summem/summem; .scratch/ never committed; v1 kept five upstreams with Screenpipe as a sidecar plus last-N facade.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"13a625ab21eb3fe9","sum":"SumMem 0.12.0 lives at .summem/summem (AGENTS.md Project Memory block is the write rule); .scratch/ is gitignored local scratch, never committed.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T170845Z-b7aad83361017857","text":"Onboarded SumMem 0.12.0 as .summem/summem (not a packages/ pin); AGENTS.md Project Memory block is the write rule.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T172705Z-bea3983b0d18183c","text":".scratch/ is gitignored local scratch (exports, dumps); do not commit it","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ab8c7585980a9874","sum":"v1 Caret keeps five upstreams (KeyType, GhostType, Computer Use Jev, Skyvern, Screenpipe); Screenpipe history is a sidecar plus last-N facade, never vendored, no TCC inherited from its CLI.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T173934Z-80f0ac884170d4c1","text":"Caret keeps five upstreams: KeyType, GhostType, Computer Use Jev, Skyvern and Screenpipe. docs/input-pipeline.md defines the proposed shared Jev/context/workflow handoff; the current action UI does not call the Python CLI.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T174647Z-c6a318f44bd68335","text":"Screenpipe history for Caret is sidecar plus facade (last N minutes/windows); do not vendor current engine or inherit TCC from their CLI","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"05674c45506c1bae","sum":"v1 Screenpipe and secrets: last-N inference hard-fails when the sidecar is down or empty; Caret supervises pinned Screenpipe via a launcher lease; Supabase is control plane only; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a7b8b39bcec29186","sum":"v1: inference needing Screenpipe last-N hard-fails when the sidecar is down or empty; CI has secret SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN, never commit its value.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T174733Z-8bbd21a4d3d18747","text":"Caret inference that needs Screenpipe history hard-fails if the sidecar is down or last-N is empty; do not continue on a miss","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T175112Z-813e2fb0e5f124b2","text":"GitHub Actions repo secret SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN is available for CI; do not commit the value.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0988f580d7d5ff22","sum":"v1: Caret launches and supervises pinned Screenpipe (TCC stays on its binary; client uses the launcher lease); Supabase only as control plane, never for last-N or threads.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T175326Z-cc8628073d6c6682","text":"Override: Caret launches and supervises pinned Screenpipe; do not spawn revoked; TCC still on their binary; client uses launcher lease","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T175517Z-d3f766ae6d1e35f4","text":"Supabase earns a seat only as company control plane (identity, entitlements, kill-switch, structured facts); skill bodies stay git/Cursor plugins; never upload last-N or threads.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"43ee91e8384e1ba6","sum":"Mac CI: keep macos-26/Xcode 26 in ci.yml (macos-15 type-checks #available); #if-gate new SDK APIs. Caret.app runs its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031, never attaching; clipboard needs --disable-clipboard-capture false; lease in .local/. No CaretProjectRoot key: supervisor no-ops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fec1309988e3870c","sum":"Mac CI runs macos-26 (Xcode 26, glassEffect): keep the Xcode 26 select in ci.yml, not macos-15 (Xcode 16.4, where #available still type-checks); #if compiler-gate new SDK APIs. Screenpipe 0.4.50 keeps no clipboard history unless --disable-clipboard-capture false.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"54b806582777cca4","sum":"2026-09-19 hackathon was happy-path only (ship, do not polish, preflight must not block on niceties). Mac CI: macos-15 defaults to Xcode 16.4 and #available still type-checks, so keep the Xcode 26 select in ci.yml and #if compiler-gate new SDK APIs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T175827Z-8c1a94d022e0b4f9","text":"2026-09-19 hackathon: GSD and happy-path only; ship, do not polish; preflight must not block on niceties","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T180736Z-4ff972dc89772e30","text":"Mac CI (macos-15) defaults to Xcode 16.4; #available is runtime-only and still type-checks. Keep the Xcode 26 select in ci.yml and #if compiler-gate new SDK APIs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3a7837f8430ada51","sum":"Mac CI on main runs macos-26 for glassEffect/Xcode 26; do not move it back to macos-15 (Xcode 16.4). Screenpipe 0.4.50 keeps no clipboard history unless --disable-clipboard-capture false; Caret's pinned launch does not pass it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T180843Z-c0da2dfb3d09eb5e","text":"Mac CI on main is macos-26 for glassEffect/Xcode 26. Do not move that job back to macos-15 default Xcode 16.4.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T181107Z-8c8e5b028a0a7d1d","text":"Screenpipe 0.4.50 stores no clipboard history by default; enable with --disable-clipboard-capture false. Caret pin launch does not pass that flag.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"82995c451c95a78f","sum":"Caret.app runs its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 (never attaches; a second recorder can stop the first); clipboard needs --disable-clipboard-capture false; last-N via .local/screenpipe-lease.json. No INFOPLIST_KEY_CaretProjectRoot: ScreenpipeSupervisor.start no-ops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"aa7dada86df3ecf0","sum":"Caret last-N reads minutes/windows/clipboard, newest first, via a lease in .local/screenpipe-lease.json. Caret.app launches screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 with clipboard on; clipboard is a Screenpipe UiEventType input, off unless --disable-clipboard-capture false.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T181331Z-7829432da9c4fa32","text":"On main 3db8f16 Caret last-N is minutes/windows via a lease; Caret.app does not spawn Screenpipe. Clipboard is a Screenpipe input UiEventType, off unless --disable-clipboard-capture false.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T182537Z-ff4a55f19dd31fc9","text":"Caret.app launches screenpipe@0.4.50 on 3031 with clipboard on and writes .local/screenpipe-lease.json. history-windows/minutes/clipboard are newest-first.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7effd9669f8097f6","sum":"Caret.app starts its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031, never attaching to a manual or launchd one (a second recorder can stop the first). INFOPLIST_KEY_CaretProjectRoot is missing from generated Info.plist, so ScreenpipeSupervisor.start is a no-op until it is added.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T183142Z-62bc24835e4cc470","text":"Caret.app always starts its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 and does not attach to a manual or launchd instance; a second recorder can stop the first.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T183914Z-5f4c9ce43ef55285","text":"INFOPLIST_KEY_CaretProjectRoot does not land in GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE output, so shipped Caret.app has no project root and ScreenpipeSupervisor.start is a no-op until that key is actually in Info.plist.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4a30ad9bb039ceab","sum":"v1: skills JSON in caret/skills/<id>/; screenpipe@0.4.50 (:3031) has its own AX prompt, /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; last-N hard-fails; xcodeproj IDs unique (Info.plist B100…62); make install needs packages/keytype.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cf173c783d21b3d2","sum":"Caret skills: JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/. Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 (launchd dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe, :3031, cli-darwin Mach-O holds TCC) has its own AX prompt, unaffected by Caret's grant. Inference last-N hard-fails. xcodeproj object IDs must be unique.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d8373d741af56a81","sum":"Caret skills: name/description JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/ (not Apify SKILL.md). Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 has its own Developer ID and AX prompt; Caret's grant does not stop it. Debug menu shows truncated last-2 via history-debug; inference last-N hard-fails.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"25648c3d0b258189","sum":"Caret skills are name/description JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/, not Apify's coding-agent SKILL.md; Apify is not a selected executor. Niko QA/Preflight (2026-09-19) used only cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh-fast or Gemini 3.8 Flash.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T185053Z-ae95c44f0be90de0","text":"Apify Agent Skills are coding-agent SKILL.md (MCP/CLI/Actors); Caret skills are name/description JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/. Apify is not a selected Caret executor.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T185221Z-b9280ccda04db89b","text":"2026-09-19: Niko QA/Preflight in this repo today must use only cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh-fast or Gemini 3.8 Flash (Gemini not on the subagent allow-list).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"458043431cd4683f","sum":"Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 has its own Developer ID (screenpipe) and its own AX prompt; granting Caret Accessibility does not stop it. Caret Debug menu shows truncated last-2 windows/minutes/clipboard via history-debug CLI; last-N hard-fail stays for inference.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T190218Z-3dcac55ddd67aa19","text":"Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 is Developer ID identifier screenpipe, not Caret; it calls AXIsProcessTrustedWithOptions and retries while waiting. Granting Caret Accessibility does not stop its dialog.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T190435Z-bd82100fe9b9695e","text":"Caret Debug menu shows truncated last-2 windows/minutes/clipboard via history-debug CLI; last-N hard-fail stays for inference.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1dc8d7a171a0b9ab","sum":"Caret runs screenpipe@0.4.50 as launchd job dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe on :3031 via the cli-darwin Mach-O (TCC is that binary); its screen/AX preflights stayed false despite Settings. Caret.xcodeproj object IDs must be unique; a FileRef in a Sources list breaks xcodebuild.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73ecfa7fb5d9e38e","sum":"Caret runs screenpipe@0.4.50 as launchd job dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe on :3031, exec'ing the cli-darwin Mach-O (TCC is that binary), not the npx shim; it logged screen=false accessibility=false and System Settings ON did not flip those preflights.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T190651Z-7c7ff0f30e9d0baa","text":"Caret-spawned screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 at 14:03 logged screen=false accessibility=false and retried VisionManager every 5s; System Settings ON did not flip those preflights.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T191856Z-e383776735c95605","text":"Caret starts screenpipe@0.4.50 as launchd job dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe on :3031; exec the cli-darwin Mach-O, not npx/node shim. TCC is that binary.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"23edfb00e1d611eb","sum":"After PR #11 (main merged), README/productContext/techContext keep launchd Screenpipe wording and the Debug last-2 preview. Caret.xcodeproj object IDs must be unique; a FileRef in a Sources files list stops xcodebuild opening the project.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T192245Z-7c3e6304f151c521","text":"PR #11 merged main; README/productContext/techContext keep launchd Screenpipe wording plus Debug last-2 preview.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T192513Z-736b08c59f95f4f1","text":"Caret.xcodeproj object IDs must be unique; a FileRef in a Sources files list makes xcodebuild unable to open the project","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"357d6a64e95bbcfa","sum":"v1: xcodeproj Info.plist B100…62 (57 TabCompletions); Screenpipe /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; vercel key is a bare token file; make install needs packages/keytype; Translate reads selection or clipboard, not the caret line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eb97d3ea4b169abf","sum":"Caret.xcodeproj Info.plist is B100…62 (57 is TabCompletions); Screenpipe 0.4.50 /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY plus X-Screenpipe-Client: api; router tests advance a fake clock past the 10 s backoff.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8b70e773b2fa893f","sum":"Caret.xcodeproj: Info.plist is B100…62, B100…57 is TabCompletions; never give Info.plist 57. Screenpipe 0.4.50 /search 403s without Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY (/health is open); Caret _api sent SCREENPIPE_API_KEY only if set.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T192920Z-0329343e8c4345de","text":"Current Caret.xcodeproj: Info.plist is B100…62; B100…57 is TabCompletions. Do not assign Info.plist 57.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T193615Z-bae439ab3f2c08e5","text":"Screenpipe 0.4.50 /search 403s without Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY; /health is open. Caret _api only sent SCREENPIPE_API_KEY if set.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0394a3f3d78f5601","sum":"Router tests advance a fake clock past the 10 s failure backoff; Caret last-N sends Bearer plus X-Screenpipe-Client: api with the token from SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY, SCREENPIPE_API_KEY, or screenpipe's own.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T193745Z-b26ffd587de72a56","text":"Router backs off RouterConfig.failure_backoff_seconds (10s) after a failed evaluation; router tests advance a fake clock rather than expecting an immediate retry. Provider presets patch their own module's post_json in tests.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T193825Z-36390ce7b0d562a4","text":"Caret last-N sends Bearer plus X-Screenpipe-Client: api; token from SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY, SCREENPIPE_API_KEY, or pinned screenpipe auth token.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8267e3a9d1defc9a","sum":"v1 keys and skills: vercel-api-gateway-key is a bare token file; make install needs packages/keytype; Debug last-N skips Caret Debug, inference last_n_windows does not; Translate reads a selection or the clipboard, never the caret line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0077b084d2383d9f","sum":"Keys and builds: vercel-api-gateway-key is a bare token file (CoreLaunchSettings envFile holds AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY/GROQ_API_KEY as KEY=value); make install needs the packages/keytype checkout or xcodebuild resolve exits 74.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T214418Z-9e6967d283b5b427","text":"vercel-api-gateway-key is a bare token file (not KEY=value); CoreLaunchSettings envFile is the KV path for AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T214943Z-7cb27000d0b12580","text":"make install requires packages/keytype checkout (CompletionUI); empty submodule dir makes xcodebuild resolve fail with 74","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f8e28d7f83c0c10b","sum":"v1 gateway skills: Debug last-N skips the Caret Debug window, inference last_n_windows does not; Translate reads a live selection or the clipboard, never the caret line.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T215111Z-04557dfeed12d63f","text":"Debug last-N windows skip title Caret Debug (matches showDebugWindow); inference last_n_windows does not skip.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T215901Z-031ebbfd04136a32","text":"Translate uses a live non-empty selection or the clipboard; it never uses the caret line. Other gateway skills still do.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bf5604878e7f35c","sum":"B1-B12: keep Chrome's titled AXWebArea out of keys; gate path writes no SQLite; never edit a running bash script; never mutate w.nodes; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; routine proof 3 silent hits Balanced, 2 Eager; Jev text goes through a SnippetLedger.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6a73d3d79df2e435","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup/AXWebArea titled (keep out of keys), web AX despite AXManualAccessibility refusal. Fixtures: makeKey(), stdin focus moves AX focus. Gate: no SQLite writes, flush on tick. findAll; 250 ms grid; powerd UserIsActive; departure once; ro .backup.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4d23ece8fc1b906f","sum":"Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX; background fixtures need makeKey(); caret-screen acts only in --act-pids. Fill recency: window before the form's last focus. Use RollingText.findAll; 250 ms tick grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0f5b9811057334dd","sum":"Reader AX lore: Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX, posts no DOM-text notices (E1/E8); background AppKit fixtures need makeKey() for focus; caret-screen acts only in --act-pids, rechecks fail closed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b99fccd1ca3e2300","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup is named after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title, so keep both out of element keys (E8); Chrome/Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) yet expose web AX, Electron accepts it; web pages post no AX notification for DOM text changes (E1).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-2317db88abe7ef57","text":"Chrome names its top AXGroup after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title; keep both out of element keys or every key moves on a title change (E8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T100848Z-7a26e801e62c7446","text":"Chrome and Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) but still expose web AX; Electron apps accept it. Web pages post no AX notification for DOM text, insert or remove changes (E1).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7284de3ea53779af","sum":"Fixtures and acting: a non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus only inside its key window (fixtures makeKey() before makeFirstResponder); caret-screen write/press act only in --act-pids, a subset of --only-pids, and rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-bac1844f3b887c52","text":"A non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus notifications only inside its key window; fixtures call makeKey() (no activation) before makeFirstResponder.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T114801Z-32531afb7e4fe1e0","text":"caret-screen write/press verbs act only in --act-pids, which must be a subset of --only-pids; without it the reader only reads. Rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfe456d6c1deaf07","sum":"Fill recency is the window before the form's last focus (the latest made Jev answer none); caret-fixture deactivates on becoming active, so poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs. RollingText.find credits the latest window: use findAll. Replay tests tick on a fixed 250 ms stream grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"55197345bf228f3c","sum":"Fill recency takes the window before the form's last focus (the latest focus made Jev answer none); caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app held the foreground, so it now deactivates on becoming active; poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T114801Z-431742a743596ba6","text":"Fill recency: take the just-left window from focus history (the window before the form's last focus), not the latest focus; latest-focus made Jev answer none on most fields once the user moved to another form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T130715Z-7922f91e68f9ff52","text":"caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app (T3 or a terminal) became the active app and held the foreground for a whole run; it now deactivates on becoming active. Poll lsappinfo front during GUI runs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"478a07b8a88c6346","sum":"Pattern code: RollingText.find credits a value seen in two windows to the most recent one; use findAll and pick the window that explains every round. Replay tests tick the helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts, or dense streams delay every transfer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-06f3c5b5c6254f49","text":"A value shown in two windows is credited by RollingText.find to the most recently seen one; pattern code must use findAll and pick the window that explains every round, or loop columns look like different sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T143157Z-9c4a82917dc22e00","text":"Replaying reader streams in tests: tick helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts; ticking only inside gaps >250 ms delays every transfer when messages are dense.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"648367d653fa1e3a","sum":"Gate path: no SQLite writes, flush on tick. Keep the pending watch's trailing debounce. No execFileSync in eval polls. Background fixture: stdin focus moves AX focus. Human input: powerd UserIsActive (B5). Count a departure once. Shadow store: ro .backup. Markers: structure.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c3649964eaa98e3b","sum":"No SQLite writes on the gate's event path (buffer, flush on tick). Pending watch: status text and a vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; keep the trailing debounce. Background-only fixture: stdin 'focus NAME' still moves AX focus. No execFileSync in eval polls.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e6572ec977c106ea","sum":"No SQLite writes on the pattern gate's event path (one insert stalled 11 ms at load 15-69); buffer and flush on tick. A --background-only caret-fixture reports no key window, yet stdin 'focus NAME' still moves AX focus; the reader sees leave and focus walks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-fc39a0364b9ecb3f","text":"Pattern gate runs on the event path: no SQLite writes there (one decision-log insert stalled 11 ms at load 15-69); decisions are buffered and flushed on tick.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T160236Z-60fc41a933501ea6","text":"A --background-only (prohibited) caret-fixture reports no key window, yet stdin 'focus NAME' (makeKey + makeFirstResponder) still moves AX focus; the reader sees leave and focus walks.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e21a3ad8c4a3fa82","sum":"Pending watch: a finished job's status text and vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; keep the trailing debounce or Jev judges a half-changed window. Eval scripts: no execFileSync in polling loops (lsappinfo every 100 ms added 150-250 ms to latencies, B4).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T160237Z-6009f034277d69a2","text":"Pending watch: a finished job's status text and its vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; without the trailing debounce the first Jev answer is about a half-changed window and is stale.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T160237Z-ba6e47628dfc0d66","text":"Eval scripts: never execFileSync in a polling loop. lsappinfo every 100 ms held the in-process helper's event loop and added 150-250 ms to every measured latency (B4).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33f4ffb90faaf6ab","sum":"Hardware input shows only as powerd's UserIsActive in pmset -g log (B5). One window departure reaches the helper up to 3 times; count it once. Read the shadow store via sqlite3 mode=ro .backup only. Pending markers come from structure, not a sidebar 'Working' text (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6aeaadf7a5a96e75","sum":"Hardware input shows only as powerd's UserIsActive in pmset -g log (B5). The helper sees one window departure up to 3 times (appSwitch, leave walk, focus elsewhere): count per departure; a return is a focused walk of a departed window.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T173801Z-d9e0d3a584c9d36e","text":"Human activity on this Mac: only powerd's UserIsActive 'kernel.useractive' in pmset -g log marks hardware input; agents' posted events raise WindowServer per-process assertions, and WindowServer per-device ones stay raised for days (B5).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T173802Z-3bfd0ad97555af7b","text":"Helper reports one window departure up to three times (appSwitch, leave walk, focus elsewhere); count per departure, and detect a return as a focused walk of a departed window, since focusedWindowId does not change across an unreadable app.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7e4af4b925d02c75","sum":"Read the shadow store only via sqlite3 'file:...?mode=ro' .backup to a temp copy (opening it as Store writes a salt). Agent sidebars (T3, Codex) keep a 'Working' status for a thread's life: pending markers come from structure, not status words (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T173802Z-57d66219a60e6cdb","text":"Read the shadow store only through sqlite3 'file:...?mode=ro' .backup into a temp copy; opening a data dir as Store creates a salt file and chmods it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201044Z-85ef58a913b9161a","text":"T3 Code and Codex list other agent threads in a left sidebar, each a button holding a status text ('Working') that lasts the thread's life; pending markers must come from structure (enabled stop button by the composer), not status words (B6 census).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9041a0b28e5b0d45","sum":"B6-B12 traps: never edit a running bash script (mv a new one over it); never mutate w.nodes; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy'; routine proof is 3 silent hits Balanced, 2 Eager; Jev text goes through a SnippetLedger.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"901960440bd057da","sum":"Helper traps B6-B9: leak-check is quadratic per line; mv a new bash script over a running one; never mutate w.nodes; pair focused:true with frontmostPid; fake-app pauses on a click; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; judge perf on real probes.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fd5a5290914f4366","sum":"Helper traps: leak-check.ts is quadratic per line (check one string per line); never edit a running bash script, mv a new one over it; never mutate w.nodes (WeakMap caches per state); focused:true from a request walk needs model.frontmostPid too.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d6128635107f5dca","sum":"Long-input traps: leak-check.ts hashes every word-bounded substring per line (quadratic; 50 KB NDJSON lines never finish, check one string per line); never edit a running bash script in place, write a new file and mv it over (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-36d6a210e08a778d","text":"leak-check.ts hashes every word-bounded substring of each line (quadratic in line length): an NDJSON with 50 KB lines never finishes; check one string per line instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201045Z-88beaae782960744","text":"Never edit a running bash script in place (bash reads it as it runs); write a new file and mv it over, as B6 did with run-audit.sh mid-audit.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"894a99a3e4795948","sum":"Screen model: apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot (candidates.ts/descriptor.ts cache per state in WeakMaps), so never mutate w.nodes; a request walk says focused:true for a background app's window, so pair model.focusedWindowId with frontmostPid.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-f95178d8fbcf4b52","text":"ScreenModel.apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot; candidates.ts and descriptor.ts cache per-state indexes in WeakMaps, so never mutate w.nodes in place.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T223858Z-64661b6aeffb7a85","text":"caret-screen's request walk (AppWorker walkWindow .request) reports focused:true for a background app's own focused window, so the helper's model.focusedWindowId alone does not mean the user is there; check model.frontmostPid (from appSwitch and frontmost focus events) too.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d3f84837adf559a9","sum":"Helper lore B8-B9: fake-app executor pauses on a click, not a key; offer expiry only in offers/lifetimes.ts; judge generator perf on real audit probes, not synthetic scenes; hand entry into a loopFinish settles first, partial matches re-offer the rest.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"364dcf1bfeba4910","sum":"Fake-app executor window is unfocused: tests pause it with a click in its frame, not a key; offer expiry lives only in offers/lifetimes.ts and records stay until offerWithdrawn (B8).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T231108Z-16725ff4ed3b6a48","text":"test/fake-app.ts's executor window is not focused, so a key userInput pauses nothing there; tests use a click inside its frame instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T231108Z-7306e773123a8d65","text":"Offer expiry lives only in helper/src/offers/lifetimes.ts: the host-offer registry keeps a record until its offerWithdrawn, and a loop going idle no longer withdraws its offers (B8).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4f388ef10e3dd3cf","sum":"Judge generator perf on real-window audit probes, not synthetic scenes (a 10x synthetic win slowed real cold calls, reverted, B8); hand entry into a loopFinish is judged after EDIT_SETTLE_MS: partial re-offers the rest under a new key, mismatch is stale (B9).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T021618Z-ea65f8fc10f79055","text":"Generator perf: judge changes by real-window audit probes (run-audit.sh PROBE_SECONDS, event-loop CPU via process.threadCpuUsage), not synthetic scenes; a row-sorted label index won 10x synthetically but slowed real cold calls (p95 5.3->7.4 ms) and was reverted (B8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T032052Z-1661c0e7f0a95c07","text":"Hand entry into a loopFinish/routine is judged after EDIT_SETTLE_MS of stillness (typing passes through prefixes): partial matches re-offer the rest under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered + replacedBy); a mismatch is stale; all entered is taken at once (B9).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cacbd4934aaf6d62","sum":"B9-B12: fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy'; routine proof is 3 silent hits at Balanced, 2 at Eager; every Jev request goes through a SnippetLedger (privacy.test); chats give under half their text, so a field takes a kind whole or not at all.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ef7f0d6980690f67","sum":"B9/B10: fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy', 'quit PID' returns it; every Jev request takes screen text through a SnippetLedger (privacy.test checks); routine proof is 3 silent hits at Balanced, 2 at Eager, off at Quiet.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2c2a04358afd7dde","sum":"Fixture --foreground takes the front in ~100 ms on 'activate legacy' and 'quit PID' returns it in ~250 ms (B9). Every Jev request takes screen text through a SnippetLedger and sets req.snippets; privacy.test fails on undeclared lines or over-budget windows (B10).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T032315Z-0691c078778b7697","text":"CaretFixture.app --foreground becomes frontmost in ~100 ms on stdin 'activate legacy' (NSApp.activate(ignoringOtherApps:)); macOS 14 NSApp.activate() never did from the background; 'quit PID' hands the foreground back within ~250 ms (B9, run-activation-proof.sh).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T043507Z-396591a0dafeb49c","text":"Every Jev request builder must take its screen text through a SnippetLedger (helper/src/privacy.ts) and set req.snippets; test/privacy.test.ts fails on any undeclared window line, over 1,200 chars from one window, or half of a non-card window (B10).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f287a62811635a9e","sum":"Routine proof follows the level (Balanced 3 silent hits, Eager 2, off at Quiet; offers/settings.ts LEVELS); tests and evals built on two hits pass settings level eager (B10).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T043510Z-072d273b831b9d6f","text":"x","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T043537Z-5d59f5b5da2447c5","text":"Routine proof follows the level (Balanced 3 silent hits, Eager 2, off at Quiet; helper/src/offers/settings.ts LEVELS); tests and evals built on two hits pass settings level eager (B10).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"71f963f682e6c288","sum":"B11-B12 chats (conversation.ts) give under half their text, at most 600 chars per Jev request; the cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks, so a field takes a kind whole or not at all, and close-on-miss stays outside kind groups (ledger charges every window showing a line).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"89eb27a1038b36eb","sum":"B11: conversations (conversation.ts) give under half their text and at most 600 chars per Jev request; the cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks (cut meeting block, Meeting date got the order's Placed date in live-replay.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T051909Z-10a9c6959d310436","text":"The conversation cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks: with calibration sources relabelled as Messages it cut the meeting block and Jev filled Meeting date with the order's Placed date (scripts/live-replay.ts, B11).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T051909Z-f82b591e5e9c3894","text":"Conversations (helper/src/conversation.ts: chat/mail bundle, composer under 3+ message lines, or stamped sender rows) give under half their text and at most 600 chars per Jev request, however short; the ledger also charges lines a taken text contains (B11).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5f02cf50c6404d08","sum":"B12 fill from chats: offer each kind a field takes whole or not at all (bare values padded the ~220-char budget and Jev picked a padding link at 0.76); privacy.test counts a line shown by any window and SnippetLedger charges per window, so keep close-on-miss outside kind groups.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T060232Z-ab20cd82e4a1331c","text":"Fill from a conversation offers each kind a field takes whole (every typed value, each with label/section/block) or not at all; letting values in bare to fit the ~220-char chat budget made Jev pick a padding thread's link at 0.76 (B12 live-run5, candidates.ts byRelevance).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T060243Z-76a84ab97345f4dc","text":"privacy.test counts a window line shown by any window's text in a request; SnippetLedger charges per window, so packing short spans after a miss pushed a 192-char chat to 104 covered on a 95 budget (B12). Keep close-on-miss outside kind groups.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"accf6d163fb02444","sum":"B13-W3: ledger charges text to each window showing it; acts need an actGrant; only hello host:true is a host; revokes immediate; Chrome AX late; swift test 2 GiB heavy lease, mutation runs --build-path /tmp; accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1, --sign-identity.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2a05f358173beb63","sum":"B13-B21: ledger charges text to every window showing it; Jev replays vary ~3 fields; acts need an actGrant; Chrome AX late, no AXSelectedText; About fills need both whose-asks; swift test: 2 GiB heavy lease; pid posts reset HIDIdleTime; Electron evals drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9f1294f6610d0c4b","sum":"B13-B17: ledger charges text to every window showing it; Jev replays vary ~3 fields; fix generator clock in load tests; acts need an actGrant; Chrome AX late, ignores AXSelectedText; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after builds; Balanced = 4 offers/hour.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d86d11223c1303db","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger charges a text to every window showing it; Jev replays vary ~3 fields, so rerun before reading a delta; socket tests bind to their own HelperServer; load-proof tests fix the generator clock; every stop carries stopReason; dry-run replays with an oracle Jev.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ea5143bf5e6179f1","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger over all windows charges a text to every window showing it; kindless fill fields withheld only on related cuts; live Jev replays vary about 3 fields, rerun before trusting a delta; socket tests bind publish to that test's own HelperServer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"15d4fcad6f30cb62","sum":"SnippetLedger over model.windows.values() charges a taken text to every window showing it, either way round, and refuses if any is over budget; a kindless fill field is withheld only on cuts of typed values or its label words, never on any cut (B13).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075125Z-769f076b2b26d50b","text":"SnippetLedger(windows) charges a taken text to every window that shows it, either way round (line inside the text, or text inside a line); refuses when any of them is over budget. Build it over model.windows.values(), never just the source window (B13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T075154Z-10f895f4b8d309e7","text":"A fill field whose label names no kind is withheld when a cut took a typed value or a cut conversation left out a line sharing its label words; withholding it on any cut blanked Name on the fill desk (unrelated team chat always cut) and lost the first-look offer (B13 live-final).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"be073912f9f26071","sum":"Live Jev replays vary by about 3 fields run to run (24-27 of 78, B13): rerun before reading a delta. Socket tests bind publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, or a late 'stopped' leaks into the next test (B14).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075211Z-5ac7a437648ff4d5","text":"Live replay noise: the same code gave 24, 26, 27 and 25 of 78 on 'sources in Messages' rule on (B13); pre-ask withholding is deterministic, so differences under about 3 fields are Jev answering differently. Rerun part with --variants/--rules/--fixes before reading a delta.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100918Z-34fd442f4a978ffa","text":"Socket test harnesses must bind the helper's publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, not the reassigned server variable: an earlier test's run timed out 5 s later and its 'stopped id-1' reached a later test's host (B13's flake, fixed B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d2825e282ce0f8d","sum":"B14: fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) in load-proof tests; names are withheld only on namesCut; every stopped taskProgress carries stopReason; try a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev before a live replay.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b51bc99b3aa533a8","sum":"B14: load-proof tests fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (find exposed ones with a wall clock jumping 1 s per read); a name field is withheld only on namesCut, since counting names prose mentions blanked Full name on Messages sets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100918Z-d51f417a758957f9","text":"Tests whose answers must not depend on CPU load fix the generator's budget clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (candidates.ts); find exposed tests by making the wall clock jump 1 s per read and rerunning the suite (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-90979468cad825fe","text":"Names are a fill kind (kinds.ts NAME_TERM): a field that takes a name is withheld only when namesCut (name-like lines or a contact line's names kept out, a partway cap/clock stop, cutAll); counting names that prose mentions blanked Full name on every Messages set (B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d0f5d3ab6d535ae7","sum":"B14: a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase); before a live replay, run a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev to see withholding and wrong fills for free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100919Z-9bbdea6cd359a808","text":"A stopped taskProgress must carry stopReason: executor progress() refuses 'stopped' at type level and stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase so the exported JSON Schema states the rule (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-aefa98c201821a3a","text":"Before a live replay, copy live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev (gold if offered, else a name-like decoy) to see withholding and wrong fills for free; B14's copy is ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b14/oracle/oracle-replay.ts.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"09651b924661b23f","sum":"B15-B17: acts need an actGrant, revoked by any pause/stop; Chrome builds web AX late and ignores AXSelectedText(Range); background WKWebView drops writes; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after fixture builds; event cards judge the last typed sentence; Balanced = 4 offers/hour.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d8e5e429dbcf056a","sum":"B15 (updated B22): the reader acts only under an actGrant from an accepted offer, revoked at once by any pause, stop or take over; Chrome builds web AX trees late and ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the walk check catches drops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"166b843e5f81c9fe","sum":"B15: any pause, stop or take over revokes the act grant at once (fakes refuse acts without one only under enforceGrants); Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds late, so wait for the form's fields in the model before acting.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124042Z-0ff3662999b3099a","text":"A stop or takeOver revokes the task's act grant at once, so a write still on its way is refused and the run ends as stopped by you; test fakes (FakeApp, SocketReader) refuse acts without a grant only when enforceGrants is set.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124042Z-b3569a4cf63d6bee","text":"Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds after the reader asks for it: wait until the form's fields are in the screen model before acting, or the first plans stop with target-not-found (B15 explore run).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ead499ab30c4256f","sum":"B15: the reader acts only under an actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s, monotonic) from an accepted offer. Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs but ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the executor's walk check catches each drop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124106Z-598a6c678d777d69","text":"caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s max, monotonic); --act-pids is for fixture tests. Only accepted offers get grants (Executor.run opts.grant); a consumer runPlan never does, so the product refuses it (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124106Z-77698db11d4c9d42","text":"Real targets (B15): Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs, front or back, but answers AXSelectedText ok and changes nothing; WKWebView in background-only caret-fixture drops value and insert silently; TextEdit takes all. The executor's walk check caught each drop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"20ef30b80edf7d92","sum":"B15-B17: Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes (insert refused); caret-fixture can't take the front from T3; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after fixture builds; event cards judge only the last typed sentence (empty body first); Balanced = 4 offers/hour (eager for a fifth).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d7fa6d069180cfdc","sum":"B15-B16: Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs, so insert is refused there; caret-fixture cannot take the front from T3; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after any swift build that changes the fixture, or evals run the old one.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T135628Z-a8acf778077d3916","text":"Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs (selection stays 0+0), so the insert fallback is refused there; and caret-fixture's 'activate legacy' cannot take the front from T3 Code, only from apps the eval launched (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T145037Z-c765ed8386dc228d","text":"Evals exec CaretFixture.app, a copy of caret-fixture made by apps/screen-reader/scripts/bundle-fixture.sh: rerun it after every swift build that changes the fixture, or the eval runs the old one (B16 lost two planner cases to an 08:33 bundle).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1148a14e8f8ea414","sum":"B17 tests: an event card judges only the last finished sentence typed (send an empty body first, then a body ending in the sentence); Balanced allows 4 offers an hour, so a test needing a fifth pop-up sets level eager first.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-a560fe18d0d7ba87","text":"Balanced allows 4 offers an hour (settings.ts LEVELS): a socket test that needs a fifth pop-up sends settings level eager first, or the gate silently holds it (B17).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f0617985abdd2b3d","sum":"B17-B21: About fills need both whose-asks (0.5); planner asks named fields only. swift test: 2 GiB heavy lease. Skill undo resets clean count; pid posts reset HIDIdleTime; background fixture ignores posted clicks; Electron evals drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2bd6c65512b6f7b3","sum":"B17-B19: typed About values fill only when both asks say the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5; planner asks only named fields; wrongKind needs a host sentence. Heavy lease 2 GiB for swift test. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell (override setters to reformat).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"28beb5cb41b23736","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev scores typed About Name/Email 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; such a value fills only when both asks call it the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16/20, 0 wrong). Planner asks only fields the instruction names; wrongKind needs a host sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0bc8adb9f0371420","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev picks typed About Name/Email at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; prompt rewordings did not help. Such a value fills only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16 of 20, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-ec0243a8194ed7a7","text":"Live Jev picks a typed About Name/Email in both asks but at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 fill cutoff, on standalone forms (B17 held-out: 1-3 of 17 filled, 0 wrong); three prompt rewordings on a dev set did not raise it (evidence/screen/b17/dev).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-3b718a56937eb180","text":"A typed About value fills only when both asks also answer the field's whose-details question as the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (fill.ts); a memory cutoff alone needed 0.6 on B18's dev set and filled 4-7 of 20, the whose question 12 of 20, held-out live 16 of 20 with 0 wrong.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8ece4134d4c0c551","sum":"B18 planner: asks only about fields the instruction names unless asksToFillForm (no field named: nothingToDo); PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind, which v2/host's exhaustive planError switch needs a sentence for.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-c901993f6e9aca54","text":"PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind (B18, kinds.ts misfit: whole address in City, email in Phone); v2/host's AskCaret.planError switch is exhaustive and needs a sentence for it at its next merge of v2/screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-d62444babaa7f479","text":"The planner asks only about fields the instruction names (relevance, or namesShortLabel for To/Cc/ID) unless asksToFillForm; an instruction that names no field, like 'msg: ...', now gets nothingToDo (B18 traded that for no unrequested writes).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94b0d9540949ad9f","sum":"Ask 2 GiB heavy leases for swift test (peaks 0.44 GB). B19 evals: copy new values each time, set offersPerHour and actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; override cell objectValue/stringValue and accessibilityValue() to reformat.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7a2abedd05327146","sum":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks 0.25-0.44 GB RSS; ask a 2 GiB lease (6 GiB is refused below ~17 GiB free). Routine evals must copy new values each time, or the closed earlier destination's text is credited as the next source and predictions miss (B19).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-db99791d758fef32","text":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks at 0.25-0.44 GB RSS (/usr/bin/time -l, B18); a 6 GiB lease estimate is refused below ~17 GiB free disk, so ask for 2 GiB.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-01ce9c46dd16673e","text":"Routine evals must copy new values each occurrence: with static source text the closed earlier destination's recent text is credited as the next source, the shape changes and predictions miss (B19; caret-fixture --windows forms, stdin form next).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"496e4b113a33f3ef","sum":"B19: real-time skill evals set offersPerHour (Eager 8/h) and writeElsewhere actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; to reformat, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and accessibilityValue() (setAccessibilityValue never fires).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-69bacc9b74bdc91c","text":"Real-time skill evals need Helper offersPerHour (Eager allows 8 offers an hour) and writeElsewhere set to actIfApproved, since a background-only fixture is never the user's window and ask first caps promotion (B19).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e6e14bbcf17c1b8d","text":"caret-fixture: AX value writes land in the NSTextField's cell and AX reads return a cached value; to reformat input, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and the field's accessibilityValue() -> String? (setAccessibilityValue never fires) (B19).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"69b2a79eea55f5b4","sum":"B19-B21: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; posted clicks reach only a --foreground caret-fixture; pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime (log last post); a closing window can arrive fieldless; drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for Electron; non-key WKWebView: focusValue.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"22bae55a2a60fd23","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; a per-pid listen-only tap sees clicks posted to that pid; background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click (use --foreground); pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime, so GUI evals log their last post.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d9542f01119cf37d","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count. A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid (global monitor and session tap do not); a background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click, --foreground (accessory) does.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e77935deee83e487","text":"Skills (B19): undoing a skill run resets its clean count, so a fixture forced-mismatch run with no Tab needs ten more clean runs after run 11's undo. Live Jev's first naming ask fell under NAME_CUTOFF 0.5 in 7 of 9 tries; the reworded retry picked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-795f3dcc958c0f2c","text":"A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid; the global NSEvent monitor and a session tap do not (B20, 6 of 6 vs 0 of 6). A background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click and cannot hit-test a covered window; --foreground (accessory) does both.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e619089820dda277","sum":"B20: input posted to a pid resets HIDIdleTime like a person's, so GUI evals record their last post (scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them. TextEdit cannot host a routine: one text area, no positions, one value per field.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-993bc2a42fa75599","text":"Input posted to a pid (CGEventPostToPid) resets HIDIdleTime like a person's (B20: 196 s to 0.3 s); GUI evals that post input record their last post (helper/scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them as 'user back'.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-ac2ee9392ce81473","text":"TextEdit cannot host a B19 routine: a shape is (source template, part, destination template) with no positions, a document is one text area, values copied from list lines share one source template, and engine.plan writes one value per field (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f76396784bf60827","sum":"B20-B21: a closing window can reach the model fieldless; routines use last-seen places. Evals starting Electron drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE. A non-key WKWebView writes AXValue to the focused field (reader: focusValue). Shadow keys are hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a097a19063cce23e","sum":"B20: a closing window can reach the model without its fields before its close, so routines place late edits from where elements were last seen; the agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, so an eval starting Electron must drop it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-5758654235cf32d7","text":"A closing window (Chrome tearing down its page, a Send that closes it) can reach the model without its fields before its close; routines place late edits and presses from where elements were last seen, or Caret's verified runs score as misses (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T004204Z-584e781bcb96f4a6","text":"The agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for its children; an eval that starts Electron must drop it or Electron runs as plain Node and cannot require('electron') (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"70fc0cfcbac83876","sum":"B20-B21: a non-key WKWebView applies an AXValue write to the focused field, so the reader focuses a web field first (focusValue); the shadow store keeps keys only as hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate and memory.sqlite routine rows are exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-9249ce81a51a9397","text":"WKWebView in a window that is not key applies an AXValue write to whichever field has focus (none: dropped; another: overwritten). The reader focuses a WebKit web field first (focusValue): 3/3 landed, no raise or activation; typing or paste to the pid land 0/3 (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-03e29f7fee084743","text":"The shadow store keeps element keys only as hashes, so an offline replay cannot recover templates or positions; scripts/real-day-replay.ts counts are approximations both ways; memory.sqlite routine rows are the faithful count (B21).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d5c81147d920ba64","sum":"B21-W3: only hello host: true is a host; revokes are immediate; reader wants a 0700 socket dir and helperAuth; swift mutation runs use --build-path /tmp; accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 under a held lock and --sign-identity; connectNative keeps the MV3 worker alive.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4593d0105bc0e4e0","sum":"B21-B23: planRequest names a window one way; only hello host: true is a host; revokes are immediate; presses only SAFE_PRESSES; --act-pids needs FIXTURE_ACTS; undo marks; reader wants a 0700 socket dir and helperAuth (launch.ts); swift mutation runs use --build-path /tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"66b7d7e70abf08e9","sum":"B21-22: planRequest window by {pid,number,title} or windowId; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; a consumer connection is a host session (evals call hostConnected); grant revoked on pause/stop; mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2f09076641c97656","sum":"B21: planRequest names a window by {pid,number,title} or windowId, never both (unread = unseenWindow); rebuild caret-screen after mutated swift tests; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; Return in a frontmost one-line field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"09ccc8ad4b5ca18a","sum":"planRequest names its window by {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; unread = unseenWindow, neither = ScreenModel.userWindow (v2/host planError needs an unseenWindow sentence). swift test on mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen: rebuild before GUI evals.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-41933c0bb214864e","text":"planRequest names its window as window {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; an unread one is unseenWindow; neither means the frontmost app's last focused window (ScreenModel.userWindow). v2/host's planError switch needs an unseenWindow sentence (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-53ebaedecebf757b","text":"swift test on a mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen; rebuild from the restored source before any GUI eval runs those binaries (B21 caught it by timestamp).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f69cdfcee30c7eb9","sum":"B21: keys posted to an inactive app's pid skip AppKit key equivalents (posted Return never ran the default button, Space pressed a focused one); frontmost, Return in a single-line field presses the default button, which the reader does not report.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-ebf44f31f7890c91","text":"A key posted to a pid whose app is not active skips AppKit key equivalents: the fixture's default button never ran on posted Return or Enter (0 of 10), Space pressed a focused button 5 of 5. The reader places key presses from cached focus and default button (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9b3d66084a009c9f","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked on close; evals call helper.hostConnected); pause/stop/settings/disconnect revoke the act grant at once, Helper.authorize before each act; mutation runs use swift test --build-path /tmp, grep 'recorded an issue'.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dc5a5754f076b1b1","sum":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks bind to it and are revoked when it closes; in-process evals must call helper.hostConnected(id). Pause, stop, settings and disconnect revoke the act grant at once; Helper.authorize is asked before each act.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccdfe7e5f11e70bf","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked when it closes; evals call helper.hostConnected). Mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps .build/debug clean; Swift Testing prints 'recorded an issue' for a failure, grep that.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b90f59e8e9d017fa","sum":"B22-B23: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS; presses only SAFE_PRESSES; only a hello with host: true is the host; undo marks give notSameElement; reader needs a 0700 socket dir and helperAuth first (launch.ts, --auth-fd); crash eval SIGKILLs a helper mid run.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e0ee3433a46919d2","sum":"B22-D2-03: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; presses only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels (risk.ts, RiskTable, press-risk.json together). Open-time event card is needsYou; only a hello with host: true is the host (evals: hostConnected).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8d97b0b1c518449c","sum":"B22: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; window ids are opaque to the helper. Presses only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels, never in a system prompt; change risk.ts, RiskTable.safePresses and press-risk.json together.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150830Z-cd56cc67608f9643","text":"B22: --act-pids now needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are <pid>-<start µs>-<generation>-<n>, opaque to the helper.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150843Z-b8f6b3671dd764ee","text":"B22: presses only whole labels in risk.ts SAFE_PRESSES / RiskTable.safePresses, never in a system prompt (subrole AXSystemDialog or AXSystemFloatingWindow, or a TCC/SecurityAgent process); change both lists and press-risk.json together.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e926b62b147229c0","sum":"D2-03: an open-time event card is needsYou with choices; a closed-line Tab re-offers it under a new key. B23: only a consumer hello with host: true is the host (v2/host must send it or no skill runs alone); in-process evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T153943Z-e96b8d822d84ddbb","text":"D2-03: an event card whose time is open (no AM/PM, no end) is figure needsYou with a choices block; the host's closed-line Tab sends no variants row, so the helper adds nothing and re-offers the card under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-0e49751b5685c975","text":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true counts as the host; other consumers bind their own work but keep no run with no Tab alive. v2/host must send host: true, or no skill runs on its own. In-process evals still call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7edb83e11969db2","sum":"B23: undo sends sameAs with a mark (reader: notSameElement otherwise; fakes test/fake-marks.ts); crash-recovery-eval SIGKILLs a helper mid run. Reader needs a 0700 socket dir; caret-screen needs --auth-fd and helperAuth first (launch.ts; evals --auth-fd 0).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"200602a89c015e6e","sum":"B23: undo sends sameAs with a mark; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element is the one it wrote (fakes: test/fake-marks.ts). crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper mid skill run; its 'helper still running' check catches crashes after the last publish.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-101e1e3d273eec2a","text":"B23: forward value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element at the key is the one it wrote (per app worker, gone on reader restart). Test fakes use test/fake-marks.ts; marks.replace(windowId, key) plays a replaced field.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-362dd90f069eee83","text":"B23: scripts/crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper child mid skill run while the script plays reader and host; its 'restarted helper is still running' check is what catches a crash after the last publish (an id collision did exactly that).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf937cd80d01ef87","sum":"B23: the reader connects only to a 0700 socket dir of the user's own (tests: mkdtemp). caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC challenge+pid); use launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0 and sendSecret.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-7971f1eeb5bd9db9","text":"B23: the reader connects only to a socket whose directory is 0700 and the user's own (never /tmp itself; HelperServer chmods its dir). Tests and evals put sockets in mkdtemp directories.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171817Z-c0fbce2e0a5b8f78","text":"B23: caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC of challenge+pid, pid = LOCAL_PEERPID). Use helper/src/launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0, sendSecret(reader, s), new HelperServer(..., s).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"861d3a8ad4100669","sum":"B23-W3: connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 under a held lock and --sign-identity; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0; person fill asks whose then values; Chrome AX shows a select's chosen option only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0a68eb7c3188c374","sum":"B23/W1/W2/I1: recovery rows return stopped with undo; open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; accept.ts under a held lock needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1; worker result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + secret.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"842e4a5a9e2cd880","sum":"B23/W1/W2: recovery.sqlite rows of runs under way return stopped with undo; react-select's chosen input has opacity 0 (walker waives it); an open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; under a held heavy lock accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"685d64f7872e343d","sum":"B23/W2: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way; at start their skills go back on Tab, rows list as stopped with undo, id generators skip ids in use. react-select sets its input opacity 0 once chosen; walker.visibleReactSelect waives opacity there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171834Z-0d54f9ef314f8bad","text":"B23: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way (skill_id in clear). At start each row's skill goes back on Tab; readable rows list as 'Stopped when Caret restarted, at step N of M' with undo. Id generators skip ids in use (idTaken).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-06db563b8bbd4ad9","text":"W2: react-select makes its input opacity 0 whenever a value is chosen, so the walker's opacity rule dropped it; walker.visibleReactSelect waives only opacity inside a visible react-select box.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"224bf2f9191d9b3d","sum":"W1/W2: open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive (360 s, CfT 154); headless CfT registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids reads it. accept.ts: page acceptance; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2154a79bf4058057","text":"W2: headless Chrome for Testing registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids <pid> reads it; accept.ts uses that for the AXManualAccessibility log check (Electron fixture via helper/scripts/electron-setup.sh).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2950b78a7b855fe8","text":"W1: an open connectNative port kept the MV3 worker alive through 360 s idle (same instance, CfT 154). Page acceptance: node fixtures/web-form/accept.ts; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7f5511b9b77cbeaa","sum":"W1/W2/I1: CfT reads NM manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; worker result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields; page.sock key is HMAC(secret,'caret-page-key'); caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + secret; golden lines are indexed 0-based on both sides.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bc66b962416e3ac5","sum":"W1/W2: CfT 154 with --user-data-dir reads NM manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome takes one command-line URL; the worker's result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields, so a new one (choice, attached, pageChanged) goes there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-9a5093647c9001cd","text":"W1: Chrome for Testing 154 with --user-data-dir reads Native Messaging manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome refuses more than one command-line URL; chrome.runtime.getFrameId is undefined in content scripts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-d139eff429d072a1","text":"W2: the worker's result() forwards only named fields of ActAnswer; a new field (choice, attached) must be added there or it silently never reaches the helper.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8a8589948371a0f4","sum":"I1: page.sock key is HMAC(launch secret,'caret-page-key'); bridge needs engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + 32-byte secret on stdin. Golden protocol.ndjson lines 60-68 are indexed 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T183627Z-67627518ce143f34","text":"I1: page.sock's key is HMAC(launch secret, 'caret-page-key') in <sock>.key, and the bridge requires engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; main.ts starts no page.sock without --auth-fd. Since B23, anything that spawns caret-screen must pass --auth-fd 0 and a 32-byte secret on stdin.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183627Z-707cb99ebedd3d58","text":"I1 golden order: protocol.ndjson lines 60-66 are B23's (hello/helperAuth/marks), 67-68 W2's pageEngine; tests index them 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"95a52729c4179521","sum":"B24/I2: person fill asks whose, then values (4 Jev calls); space Groq writer calls 30 s; Chrome AX shows a select as AXPopUpButton, chosen option only. W3: Helium reads NativeMessagingHosts in a temp profile; accept.ts needs --sign-identity, boots a launchd testhost.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a993ea246e3968f1","sum":"B24/I2: a person's fill asks whose, then values (4 Jev calls, PER_FILL); space Groq writer calls 30 s; TextEdit opens CLI files only from its container tmp; Chrome AX shows a select as AXPopUpButton with only its chosen option; toWindowSnapshot mirrors Chrome AX.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d32f644355f794d8","sum":"B24: a fill asks whose first, then values: 4 Jev calls (tests use PER_FILL); space Groq writer calls 30 s; sandboxed TextEdit opens a command-line file only from ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-05aef102d22989aa","text":"B24: fill asks in two stages when a field takes a person's details (whose first, then values), so a fill is 4 Jev calls, not 2; tests that count calls use PER_FILL. Groq's qwen3.8 hits 429 token limits within ~20 plans; space writer calls 30 s.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T192504Z-2947a2d88b908a7e","text":"B24: TextEdit is sandboxed: a file named on its command line opens only from inside ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp (realfill-capture.ts makes its own folder there and deletes it).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"712d8e92089c7858","sum":"B24/I2: Chrome AX shows a native select as AXPopUpButton holding only its chosen option, so fill hands selects off; page-link toWindowSnapshot mirrors Chrome AX (AXTimeField; radios in an AXGroup per name; options as AXMenuItem).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-d09a0e8b1bd722e1","text":"B24: Chrome's AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton whose only child is the selected option; the option list is not readable without opening it, so fill names selects as hand-offs with no value (capture-2 probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195842Z-c30fb40a821e024f","text":"I2: page-link.ts toWindowSnapshot must match Chrome AX for fill/controls.ts: time is AXTimeField, radios sit under an AXGroup per name attribute, select options are AXMenuItem children. PageControl has no fieldset legend, so page radio groups have no label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0581e9c7aa2f84db","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp profile, reads NativeMessagingHosts there; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid. Bridge reaches host over XPC; accept.ts needs --sign-identity/--other-identity, boots a temp launchd testhost. Headless CfT: createTarget steals focus","tree":{"c":[{"id":"13ae7e710e2343cf","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp profile and reads NativeMessagingHosts there; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid so a swapped socket can't relay the host's hello.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-5a96910dba2d6b69","text":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads Native Messaging manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts (accept.ts --browser passes 42/42); its Web Store page offers Add to Helium.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-74ab7d13fad22cf2","text":"W3: page.sock proofs both bind the helper pid (bridgeProof too), or a same-user process that swaps the socket path can pass the host's hello to the real helper and keep that session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94d9cdb89929ed3f","sum":"W3: bridge reaches host over XPC (no page.sock key); accept.ts needs --sign-identity/--other-identity, boots a temp launchd testhost. Headless CfT: createTarget steals focus, activateTarget won't return it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-903b513efe20fc90","text":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the Caret host over XPC (CaretBridgeXPC), never page.sock; no <sock>.key exists. accept.ts needs --sign-identity <team SHA-1> (and --other-identity for refusal checks) and runs caret-bridge-testhost as a temporary launchd job it boots out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-98052ff285eab267","text":"W3: headless Chrome for Testing gives focus to a window CDP Target.createTarget opens and Target.activateTarget does not move it back; chrome.windows focused is reported in headless. Page window focus = active tab of the focused, last-focused window.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
